// component helper functions- functions that are inside a component and are used to carryout specific logic ( it determines the component's behaviour!!)
//  destructuring- extract individual values into variables  from objects and arrays so that we can easily use them -> we have 3 ways of destructuring

// 🥷✅DYNAMIC NOT STATIC WEBPAGES!!
// Page-rendering-> after the initial rendering,we can use stateful components to do that
// re-render components = STATE
// A state(variable) that changes or could change during the lifecycle of a component

// NB: If any state(or any variable with in the component) changes, the component will re-render
// Every time the setCounter modifies the state it causes the component to re-render

//  --EVENT HANDLING--
//  User interacting with different elements of the web page can cause a collection of various kinds to be triggered


// 1st option
let counter = 1;
// normal rendering
const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById("root"));
// put it in a function
const refresh = () => {
  root.render(<App counter={counter} />);
};
// For the initial or the first time,value=1 , it re-renders 1st time
refresh();
// lets manually change the value of the counter variable, so now its changed
counter += 1;
// call the function to see the change in value of the counter variable,value=2, it re-renders 2nd time
refresh();
// have to manually change the counter variabl, so now its changed
counter += 1;
// call the function again so that we can see change in value of the counter variable, value=3, it re-renders 3rd time
refresh();

// 2nd option- since the code is in a synchronous format, the displays with have such a short amount of time, because after each function is call
// once, the second function is also called sequentially
// -lets take control of how we want our components to be re-render, so we will want the change of the  value or re-rendering to happen after every
// second , so that we can have time to see the displays - lets use setInterval function
setInterval(() => {
  refresh();
  counter += 1;
}, 1000);
// the setInterval function will loop continuously until we can specify to stop!!

// Making repeated calls of the render function isnt necessarily the best way to re-render our components, best its manually and wont work for
// if want to re-render or change the value of a certain variable many times!! - lets use state [React state hooks]
// -A state is just a variable that will change its value during the lifecycle of the component- any variable that you know will change later on
// should be considered as state

// setCounter function cause the component to re-render every its called as long as the application runs
